/borge
/bin/
/dist/
/.venv-borg2/
/tests/evidence/out/
*.zip
*.test
*.prof
coverage.out
/tests/borg2/borg2
/internal/*/testdata/fuzz/

# Python bytecode. The repo runs CPython in three places - the borg 2 reference
# interpreter, the fixture generators, and the differential tests that compare against
# CPython's own strftime and stat - and every one of them is invoked with
# PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 so these never appear. Ignored anyway: a stray __pycache__
# committed into a Go repository is noise nobody looks at twice.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
